          "version": 6
        },
        "fields": {
          "notes": "Work identity follows the current GND authority. Exact source-backed regions in mixed W II notebooks are identified at region and inscription-layer level. D 21 / GSA 71/28 is Nietzsche's autograph print manuscript for E 42, but later additions, Köselitz's title suggestion and Nietzsche's adoption, proof-stage insertions, and the late migration of Was ich den Alten verdanke remain distinct events. The existing unlabelled 1889-dated Naumann Item was printed and received by Nietzsche in November 1888. The Köselitz-edited 1893 second edition contains textual changes made after Nietzsche’s participation ended. The provisional Russian translation has its own expression identity and awaits textual assessment."
        },
